node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log

# `dist/app.js` and `dist/styles.css` are generated, and are deliberately NOT
# ignored. Both are committed so that `node build.mjs` alone rebuilds the page
# on a fresh checkout with nothing but Node, which is the property the build's
# zero-dependency rule exists to protect. Adding either here would break that.
# CI byte-compares both against a fresh `npm run compile`, so a stale copy is
# caught rather than shipped.

# Working copies of upstream food-composition datasets. They are large, and
# redistributable only under their own terms, so they are fetched rather than
# committed. `tools/usda.mjs` downloads SR Legacy on demand; the flavonoid
# release that `tools/flavonoids.mjs` reads is downloaded by hand, as the README
# describes.
tools/cache/

# Scratch space for the plan-execution tooling in docs/superpowers: ledgers,
# task briefs and review packages, all of which describe work whose record is
# the git history itself.
.superpowers/

# Isolated worktrees for branch work. The checkouts inside are the same
# repository seen from another directory, and committing them into it would
# nest the tree inside itself.
.worktrees/
